WEBVTT

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.940
You don't look very happy, Eizan-kun.

00:00:05.940 --> 00:00:07.570
What are you talking about?

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:09.440
The arena's really pumped.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:11.650
This year's Autumn Selection is a major success.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:14.160
As the organizers, 
we have nothing to be unhappy about.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.910
But it looks very different from how you imagined it to be, doesn't it?

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.540
Hmph.

00:00:20.540 --> 00:00:22.370
I have no idea what 
you're talking about.

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:27.090
You're the one who directed Mimasaka Subaru 
to target Souma-kun, aren't you?

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.500
If he crushed Takumi-kun,

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:31.970
Souma-kun would no doubt agree 
to the Cooking Battle.

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:36.090
If he were defeated before such a large crowd without being able to avenge his friend,

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.350
there would be no greater humiliation.

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:41.720
You kept your hands clean and manipulated everything from behind the scenes.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:45.060
It's very much your style, Eizan-kun.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.190
However, your schemes didn't work.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.610
You used your wits to set up a trap
 the best you knew how,

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:55.110
but maybe you're the one who got caught and drowned instead.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.570
What did you just say?!

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:58.830
I'd like you to have seconds too.

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.330
Does no one want more?

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:04.460
It's the end of the line.

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.920
With this, we conclude the evaluation—

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:10.340
If it means you'd have seconds,

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.170
I'd like you to pour this 
over the rice and dig in.

00:01:17.010 --> 00:01:19.550
Well, to be more precise,

00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:21.350
it wasn't only you.

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:25.230
Everyone at Tohtsuki 
probably felt the same way.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.980
My Pacific saury dish is not yet complete.

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.320
<i>That's...</i>

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.990
<i>a white soup?</i>

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:58.640
Far beyond the image I have in my mind

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:05.110
The reality I'm building up is still far away

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.860
An endless journey

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:13.870
Let's hone each other's pride

00:02:13.870 --> 00:02:16.370
Words aren't really important

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:18.870
So let's just say "yes" and leave it at that

00:02:18.870 --> 00:02:25.840
We fight each other and hone our skills

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:30.720
Our encounters cause shockwaves

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:33.470
We're reckless challengers

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:38.470
Heading toward a world as yet unexplored

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:41.020
A swordsman should use his blade

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:43.850
To open the way to the future

00:02:43.850 --> 00:02:49.570
This is my story and no one else's

00:03:07.950 --> 00:03:09.910
Let's have seconds.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:17.670
Yukihira-kun, you're free to
 struggle on till the very end,

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:22.930
but isn't this just a remake of the idea you used in your match against me?!

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:25.010
<i>No, it's not, Alice.</i>

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:26.100
<i>It's—</i>

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:27.890
There, honored judges.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:29.480
This is my Pacific saury dish:

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.150
Porridge-Style Pacific Saury Rice.

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:33.900
Enjoy!

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:40.610
<i>The slightly viscous soup</i>

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.070
<i>has soaked into the dish</i>

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.070
<i>and gently melded with the rice.</i>

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:55.330
There he goes!

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.590
Bare-chested!

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:00.170
Mild and creamy...

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:04.140
This white soup is soy milk!

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:05.600
That's right.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:09.810
I gradually added miso and just a touch of Parmesan cheese to the soy milk,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:12.140
then slowly simmered it 
until the soup became warm.

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:13.770
Soy milk?

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.900
You noticed, Alice.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.230
The critical component of porridge is the broth.

00:04:19.730 --> 00:04:23.740
He used soy milk as the broth and built his dish on that foundation.

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.700
I see.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:29.870
<i>Broth is essentially umami itself.</i>

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:33.750
<i>Like kelp, soy milk contains
 large quantities of glutamic acid.</i>

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.960
<i>It's more than qualified to serve as the base for the porridge's flavor.</i>

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.380
<i>Further, umami components 
have a synergistic effect.</i>

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.430
<i>When two are present, the resultant umami 
is far more than the sum of its parts.</i>

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.220
<i>The inosinic acid from Pacific saury</i>

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:47.970
<i>and the glutamic acid from soy milk...</i>

00:04:47.970 --> 00:04:50.100
<i>Combining the two makes total sense.</i>

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.060
A soy milk porridge.

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.350
How interesting.

00:04:56.480 --> 00:05:01.730
<i>There are ingredients that have suddenly become prominent by adding the soup, as well.</i>

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.740
What's mixed into the rice?

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:05.990
Crunchy pickled plums.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:06.490
What?!

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:07.370
Crunchy pickled plums?

00:05:07.370 --> 00:05:08.030
What?!

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:09.450
Not common snacks again?!

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:12.290
These plums serve as important accents.

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.710
The crunchy mouthfeel is fun,
 adding vivid visual impact!

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:19.170
For the taste buds, the plums help cut through the fattiness of the Pacific saury and provide a refreshing aftertaste.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.670
The dish makes full use of the acidity's ability to increase appetite.

00:05:22.670 --> 00:05:25.970
The plums were pickled in salt.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.180
They are the perfect choice 
to complement the aged Pacific saury!

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:31.970
Another item of note 
is the Parmesan cheese in the soup.

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:33.890
This Western ingredient is combined with Japanese ingredients,

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:36.270
such as the salted rice-bran Pacific saury, 
pickled plums, and miso,

00:05:36.270 --> 00:05:38.940
to create a brand new flavor!

00:05:38.940 --> 00:05:44.240
<i>It reminds me of when I met my beloved.</i>

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:47.410
<i>This way.</i>

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:53.910
<i>An encounter made possible by two 
that have developed</i>

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:55.620
<i>in different countries and cultures.</i>

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:57.210
<i>A most unique encounter.</i>

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:00.040
You've got to be kidding.

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:01.920
That's high praise right there.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:04.550
Who knew that the transfer student would...

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:08.090
Did you see this <i>Tohtsuki Spotlight</i> issue?

00:06:08.090 --> 00:06:09.470
According to the journalism club,

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:13.220
they can sell more copies when they write an article bashing Souma-kun.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:14.680
Of course they would.

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:18.230
He publicly said that this academy's just a stepping stone for him.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.850
You can tell from the audience's reaction too.

00:06:20.270 --> 00:06:23.270
They dislike him not just from afar
 but in person as well.

00:06:23.270 --> 00:06:24.320
Is that really true?

00:06:24.900 --> 00:06:27.650
I don't think that's the only reason.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:31.700
He had a very close spice match with Hayama-kun in the prelims.

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:35.700
In the main tournament, he defeated Alice-kun,
 a relative of the Devil of Food.

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:40.500
Furthermore, he overcame Mimasaka-kun, a monster who'd been undefeated in 99 Cooking Battles.

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:44.710
Yet many students don't want
 to acknowledge Souma-kun.

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:46.420
Why is that?

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.930
Souma-kun's father 
told me something once.

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:51.640
<i>Dad!</i>

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.970
<i>I'm gonna become a chef 
who can beat you, Dad!</i>

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.930
<i>Oh, yeah?</i>

00:06:56.930 --> 00:06:58.230
<i>Well, good luck.</i>

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:58.930
<i>Okay!</i>

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.440
<i>Let's do a cooking match right now!</i>

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.820
In my eyes, Souma didn't have 
any special cooking skill.

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:09.610
Kids say that sort of thing,

00:07:09.610 --> 00:07:13.120
so I thought he'd have enough once I beat him a couple of times.

00:07:13.740 --> 00:07:17.500
But Souma never let himself get down.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.460
Every time, he gets one step closer.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:22.960
One day, I realized something.

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:27.960
Souma lacks something any 
normal person would have.

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:29.670
And what is that?

00:07:30.300 --> 00:07:32.430
See, everyone wants to believe

00:07:32.430 --> 00:07:36.390
that it's normal to do worse
 than someone who has talent.

00:07:36.390 --> 00:07:38.930
That way, they lower their expectations

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:42.310
and protect their pride, self-respect, and similar sorts of things.

00:07:43.310 --> 00:07:45.310
But Souma doesn't do that.

00:07:45.730 --> 00:07:49.320
He has the strength 
to face his inadequacies head-on.

00:07:49.740 --> 00:07:53.660
That's an incredible strength 
that even I don't have.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.660
Souma-kun's cooking inspirations

00:07:56.660 --> 00:08:00.040
aren't from natural genius 
or anything like that.

00:08:00.040 --> 00:08:01.160
He just thinks things through.

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:04.130
He keeps testing and retesting his recipes.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:07.500
Everyone can do that,
 but not everyone actually does.

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:09.170
<i>I bet it won't work.</i>

00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:12.130
<i>He's up against Hayama Akira,
 who has a superhuman sense of smell.</i>

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.800
<i>Kurokiba Ryou is an elite who was
 handpicked by the Nakiri family too.</i>

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:16.800
<i>A way to {win against}beat them?</i>

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:18.600
<i>I wouldn't even bother thinking one up.</i>

00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:19.930
<i>It's impossible.</i>

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:22.100
<i>Of course the genius will win.</i>

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:26.110
Why did they want to 
think less of Souma-kun?

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:28.020
Because if they acknowledged him,

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:30.820
it'd mean acknowledging 
their own lack of effort.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:36.530
But the tide's about to turn.

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:37.740
He's amazing!

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:38.200
Yeah.

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:41.370
He's playing against those 
two monsters at <i>their</i> level!

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:42.710
He might be able to do this.

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.670
After this, I can't help but acknowledge him.

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:46.920
<i>Yukihira...</i>

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:47.750
<i>Yukihira.</i>

00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:48.540
<i>Yukihira!</i>

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:49.420
<i>Yukihira.</i>

00:08:49.420 --> 00:08:50.630
<i>Yukihira Souma is...</i>

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.590
<i>...amazing!</i>

00:08:57.140 --> 00:08:58.050
Glad you liked it!

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:01.020
With this, we conclude the evaluation!

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.100
And now, the verdict!

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:10.940
Oh, c'mon.

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:12.940
Well? What is it?

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.030
I'm sure it'll be okay!

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:14.950
He can do it!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:15.910
He can!

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:16.990
Souma-kun...

00:09:21.160 --> 00:09:22.620
<i>Yukihira...</i>

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:25.660
<i>After closing the gap in ingredient quality,
 you even managed to make a dish of that caliber.</i>

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:27.500
<i>Interesting.</i>

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:29.630
<i>You're really interesting, Yukihira.</i>

00:09:31.380 --> 00:09:34.420
<i>Good or bad, this is the final result.</i>

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:35.930
<i>This is it!</i>

00:09:35.930 --> 00:09:37.930
First, well done.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.810
Each of you presented your unique strengths well,

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:44.930
in a clash befitting the grand finale.

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:46.810
First, regarding your cooking techniques,

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.560
all three of you are on par.

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.020
Next, regarding your ability
 to judge ingredient quality,

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:54.990
Kurokiba and Hayama are clearly exceptional.

00:09:54.990 --> 00:09:58.450
They made the perfect choices
 when selecting their Pacific saury.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:03.330
However, Yukihira has closed the gap
 through his creativity.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:07.210
His inventiveness is exceptional among the three!

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:10.040
Great!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.630
Even more surprisingly,

00:10:12.630 --> 00:10:16.420
all three dishes had flavors that were nearly equal.

00:10:19.390 --> 00:10:22.140
However, the deciding factor

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:25.100
was how well the dish reflected
 the chef as an individual.

00:10:26.020 --> 00:10:28.350
The chef as an individual?

00:10:28.350 --> 00:10:30.350
That's right, Yukihira-kun.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:33.570
A dish brimming with true originality

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:39.030
allows you to picture the chef in your mind just by tasting the dish.

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:40.450
Put differently,

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:42.410
it's a dish with such originality

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.870
that only one specific chef could've created it.

00:10:44.870 --> 00:10:51.130
As a sign of respect, we call 
such a dish the chef's specialty.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:53.210
The one who deserves victory

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:56.510
is the chef who best pursued his own cooking!

00:10:56.510 --> 00:11:00.760
The chef who truly sought what his cooking should look like!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:04.720
And that person's name is...

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:19.240
<i>I don't know what my parents look like or what my real name is.</i>

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.610
<i>All I know</i>

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:25.530
<i>is that I was abandoned as a newborn in the outskirts of the slum.</i>

00:11:25.530 --> 00:11:29.040
You deserve better than this.

00:11:29.460 --> 00:11:32.580
Your sense of smell may remake the world itself!

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:42.680
<i>It was Shiomi Jun who pulled me out of the slums.</i>

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:47.060
<i>Professor Hayama, 
who was Jun's advisor at the time,</i>

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:48.890
<i>agreed to become my legal guardian.</i>

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:54.020
<i>They chose my name to indicate 
someone who would bring</i>

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:55.810
<i>a new world of cooking to light.</i>

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:57.730
<i>I was named Akira.</i>

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.860
<i>Jun was always by my side.</i>

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:20.760
Akira-kun is a very good boy.

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.380
He's so earnest in helping with my research.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:26.760
He helps compensate for what I lack.

00:12:26.760 --> 00:12:29.140
I can't thank him enough, really.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:30.770
But...

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.350
I'm scared.

00:12:33.350 --> 00:12:35.020
I'm scared that for my own sake,

00:12:35.020 --> 00:12:38.150
I'm making Akira-kun do something he doesn't really want to do.

00:12:39.480 --> 00:12:40.320
<i>No.</i>

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:43.320
<i>That's not true, Jun.</i>

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:46.070
<i>You saw something in me... My true worth.</i>

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:51.080
You deserve better than this.

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.870
<i>You gave me a reason to live!</i>

00:12:53.870 --> 00:12:56.830
<i>You're the one who brought me into the light.</i>

00:12:57.210 --> 00:13:00.210
<i>I have to win for Jun.</i>

00:13:00.590 --> 00:13:02.340
<i>This isn't good enough!</i>

00:13:03.220 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>My cooking's meaningless
 unless I can win using a method</i>

00:13:05.840 --> 00:13:07.430
<i>that no one else can copy.</i>

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.100
<i>I will change the world of taste through the power of fragrance.</i>

00:13:11.100 --> 00:13:13.480
<i>That's my cooking.</i>

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:18.020
<i>I'll give everything I have to offer to this one dish!</i>

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:24.110
The victor...

00:13:24.820 --> 00:13:26.660
is Hayama Akira!

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.130
Hayama!

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.420
It's Hayama!

00:13:41.050 --> 00:13:43.550
Seared Pacific Saury Carpaccio.

00:13:43.550 --> 00:13:46.630
The dish was worthy of being called a specialty.

00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.640
Congratulations, Hayama-kun!

00:13:56.890 --> 00:13:58.440
Congratulations.

00:13:58.440 --> 00:13:59.400
Congratu...

00:14:00.020 --> 00:14:02.360
You did it, Hayama-kun!

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.320
I'm so happy for you! So happy.

00:14:05.320 --> 00:14:07.780
Ugh, you always keep your cool.

00:14:07.780 --> 00:14:09.620
You should act a little happy!

00:14:10.370 --> 00:14:10.990
For winnin—

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:16.790
Huh?!

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.630
Akira-kun, wh-what's wrong?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.590
N-Nothing!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:29.220
Akira-kun, the smell of cinnamon 
is said to cheer you up.

00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:33.890
<i>I see.</i>

00:14:34.850 --> 00:14:36.680
<i>His expression during the semi-finals.</i>

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.100
<i>I'm the one who'll climb to the top!</i>

00:14:40.100 --> 00:14:41.810
<i>I won't let anyone else get close!</i>

00:14:42.310 --> 00:14:45.030
<i>That wasn't a smile of confidence.</i>

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:46.820
<i>It was to rouse himself.</i>

00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.990
<i>It was almost as though 
he was threatening himself.</i>

00:14:49.700 --> 00:14:50.950
How fragile.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:51.530
What?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:54.830
Hayama-kun, that was a wonderful dish.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:56.660
Thank you, Chef Doujima.

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:59.000
But too great a talent

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.330
will turn against itself in the end.

00:15:02.250 --> 00:15:06.090
I hope that you will be able to maintain a good relationship with your talent.

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:11.340
Ryou-kun!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.260
Jeez! Jeez, jeez, jeez, jeez, jeez!

00:15:14.260 --> 00:15:17.100
I can't believe you lost right in front of me!

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:19.350
Jeez, jeez, jeez, jeez, jeez!

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:19.350
Hey, that hurts.

00:15:19.350 --> 00:15:21.310
What's that for, bitch?!

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.310
Oh?!

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:23.650
How dare you call your master a bitch?

00:15:23.650 --> 00:15:24.770
We're through!

00:15:24.770 --> 00:15:26.690
You can apologize to me once you feel sorry!

00:15:28.780 --> 00:15:31.910
<i>I'm gonna become a chef who can beat you!</i>

00:15:32.450 --> 00:15:33.030
<i>Hm?</i>

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:34.870
<i>Hey, Souma.</i>

00:15:34.870 --> 00:15:36.450
<i>That sardine is no good.</i>

00:15:36.450 --> 00:15:36.910
<i>Huh?</i>

00:15:38.620 --> 00:15:42.080
<i>Don't lose to anyone else
 before you lose to me next time.</i>

00:15:45.750 --> 00:15:46.750
Hayama.

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:49.880
Can you make more of that carpaccio?

00:15:49.880 --> 00:15:51.470
I guess I still have the ingredients.

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:52.300
Let me have a taste.

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:53.390
Huh?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:54.760
Why?

00:15:54.760 --> 00:15:56.310
Let me have some.

00:15:56.310 --> 00:15:57.850
Uh, but it takes some work—

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.770
Let me try it too, bastard!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:02.690
Why're you acting like
 you're trying to start a fight?

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:07.820
What's with you two?

00:16:08.900 --> 00:16:11.280
I would've been able to make it better.

00:16:11.280 --> 00:16:13.070
Huh? A sore loser, I see.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:14.410
Listen.

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.030
Tonight decided the first-years' 
preliminary rankings.

00:16:17.490 --> 00:16:19.830
Among us here, I'm the top seat.

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:22.830
You should show me respect from now on.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.460
Want to have a rematch right now?!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.210
Sure.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:27.920
The results still won't change.

00:16:27.920 --> 00:16:28.920
Now, now.

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:32.340
Hayama, you made a pretty good dish too.

00:16:32.340 --> 00:16:35.180
Why're you talking down to me, third place?

00:16:35.180 --> 00:16:37.390
You don't know that!

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:38.470
Don't make things up!

00:16:38.760 --> 00:16:40.770
You're saying I ranked below you?!

00:16:40.770 --> 00:16:41.930
Don't yell while eating!

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:44.270
But yours was good too, Hayama.

00:16:44.270 --> 00:16:47.610
Maybe there's nothing 
to worry about with Hayama.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:51.150
Those three look to become an interesting trio.

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:53.820
Right.

00:16:53.820 --> 00:16:57.280
Diamonds in the rough collide, 
polishing each other.

00:16:57.280 --> 00:16:59.990
That's exactly what Tohtsuki is all about.

00:16:59.990 --> 00:17:05.120
Indeed. Tonight, yet another 
new gem has been created!

00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:41.830
Souma-kun, that was really good work!

00:17:41.830 --> 00:17:45.580
Okay, tonight, we celebrate 
Yukihira finishing second!

00:17:45.580 --> 00:17:46.830
Let's party!

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:48.330
Yeah, in Marui's room!

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:50.290
Why is it always my room?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:51.670
Because it's big, okay?

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:52.420
Crap!

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:54.590
Sorry, can you guys go ahead?

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.180
What do you want, Dad?

00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:00.970
Hey, Souma.

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:02.180
Been a while.

00:18:02.680 --> 00:18:03.520
Well?

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:05.350
How'd the main tournament go?

00:18:05.350 --> 00:18:07.480
Oh, well.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:08.100
So...

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.810
Aw! You lost, huh?!

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:11.940
Who won?

00:18:12.320 --> 00:18:13.610
Hayama.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:15.490
Oh, Shiomi's disciple, huh.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.490
Get it together, yeah?

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:20.030
It's like I lost to Shiomi.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:21.410
<i>Shit.</i>

00:18:21.410 --> 00:18:24.240
<i>He's so upbeat when he's making fun of me.</i>

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:27.210
<i>What kind of parent feels happy 
when their son loses?</i>

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.580
Well, but to be fair,

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.340
if you can perfect fragrance, it's amazing.

00:18:32.340 --> 00:18:34.340
No, that wasn't all there was to it.

00:18:34.670 --> 00:18:36.630
In his dish...

00:18:37.510 --> 00:18:39.550
<i>I sensed overwhelming tenacity.</i>

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:42.550
Dad, I'm glad I left Yukihira.

00:18:43.310 --> 00:18:46.890
If I hadn't, I wouldn't have 
noticed all these things.

00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:52.940
So, I'm going to explore
 the kind of cooking only I can do.

00:18:52.940 --> 00:18:53.770
If I don't do that,

00:18:53.770 --> 00:18:56.820
there's no point in my carrying
 on the family business.

00:18:57.400 --> 00:18:57.780
Huh?

00:18:57.780 --> 00:18:59.450
Now that I've said it,

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:01.990
that doesn't sound that different 
from what I've been doing already.

00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:02.740
Well...

00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.240
Why not? Be that way.

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:10.330
<i>Was that a yawn?</i>

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:11.290
Bye.

00:19:12.710 --> 00:19:14.840
<i>He's finally met someone his age</i>

00:19:14.840 --> 00:19:17.670
<i>who can blow who he is now
 out of the water, huh?</i>

00:19:18.880 --> 00:19:20.840
<i>That's right, Souma.</i>

00:19:21.430 --> 00:19:22.760
<i>Meet them.</i>

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:27.060
<i>Only through these encounters
 can a chef move forward.</i>

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:30.230
<i>If you face a dish on your own,</i>

00:19:30.940 --> 00:19:33.810
<i>you'll only see the same self as before.</i>

00:19:36.270 --> 00:19:40.150
My own cooking, huh.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:08.980
An intensely burning desire was born

00:20:08.980 --> 00:20:14.820
But not in me, in someone else

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:19.620
Where's the me who believed that

00:20:19.620 --> 00:20:24.750
All one needs is to have hopes and dreams

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:30.000
Wrapped around something long, my compass was lost

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:35.760
On the border of life and death, snow drops bloom

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:41.100
If by some mistake they get smashed

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:46.270
At least put flowers on the empty husk

00:20:46.270 --> 00:20:51.940
Is that the way things are? Yes, it is

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:56.990
You can call it resignation if you want

00:20:56.990 --> 00:21:02.910
But that's not me, that's not me

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:07.540
There's no value in something just anyone could make

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:12.620
Hiya!

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:14.120
Nikumi-cchi!

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:14.870
Welcome!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:16.670
Thanks for the text.

00:21:16.670 --> 00:21:18.540
You got a shipment of good game meat?

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:19.210
Nice!

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:20.750
Looks tasty!

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:21.880
Here.

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:24.420
It's one of mine, but it looks good on you!

00:21:24.420 --> 00:21:26.130
Oh, thank you, Megumi.

00:21:26.130 --> 00:21:28.350
All right, let's start!

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:29.300
Yeah!

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:30.390
How nice.

00:21:30.390 --> 00:21:34.100
Lovely girls in a kitchen working together in harmony.

00:21:34.100 --> 00:21:37.690
It doesn't appear so lovely 
when you actually look at it, though.

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:40.440
By the way, where's Yukihira?

00:21:40.440 --> 00:21:42.650
Oh, he's back there today.

00:21:43.070 --> 00:21:45.820
So, the mellow soy milk flavor

00:21:45.820 --> 00:21:49.870
enhances the gentle saltiness of the Pacific saury in a good way.

00:21:49.870 --> 00:21:53.040
Still, crunchy pickled plums feel too cheap

00:21:53.040 --> 00:21:54.540
for me to want to eat them.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:56.000
But you're shoveling it in
 like you like it!

00:21:56.710 --> 00:21:57.420
Seconds.

00:21:57.420 --> 00:21:58.580
And you want another serving?

00:21:58.580 --> 00:22:02.460
The cartoccio I made for you
 yesterday was better, though.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.170
Huh?!

00:22:03.170 --> 00:22:05.380
Then try making it again!

00:22:05.380 --> 00:22:06.470
Let's compare!

00:22:06.470 --> 00:22:09.300
Whatever, but why are you guys
 taste-testing at our place?

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:10.680
I made tea!

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:11.100
What?!

00:22:11.100 --> 00:22:12.720
You don't have to play hostess, Jun.

00:22:13.220 --> 00:22:16.430
And why're you offering such high-quality cookies?

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:18.440
They'll be fine with cheap snacks!

00:22:18.440 --> 00:22:19.810
Hey, we can hear you.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:22.400
You're a skinflint and a nagger too.

00:22:19.810 --> 00:22:23.730
<i>The specialty... a dish that shows the chef's character.</i>

00:22:22.400 --> 00:22:24.230
That's because you're such a pig.

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:27.240
<i>What Hayama's cooking has, but mine lacks.</i>

00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:29.740
Hey! Don't cram them all into your mouth!

00:22:29.740 --> 00:22:30.240
Hayama!

00:22:31.030 --> 00:22:33.160
I want to compare dishes.

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:35.250
One Seared Pacific Saury Carpaccio, thanks.

00:22:35.250 --> 00:22:36.160
Make that two.

00:22:36.160 --> 00:22:37.910
Shut up. Go home.

00:22:37.910 --> 00:22:39.000
Two on the double, yeah?

00:22:39.000 --> 00:22:40.670
You guys!

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:43.090
Yukihira's crazy,

00:22:43.090 --> 00:22:45.460
spending all that time with someone he lost to.

00:22:45.460 --> 00:22:46.210
Yeah.

00:22:46.210 --> 00:22:47.720
Isn't he frustrated by the results?

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:51.970
I'm sure Souma-kun feels more frustrated than we'll ever know.

00:22:51.970 --> 00:22:53.390
That's why he's there all the time.

00:22:53.720 --> 00:22:57.100
But to know who you really are,

00:22:57.100 --> 00:23:00.520
you must step outside the world you know.

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:04.770
Even if that means facing the one who got the better of you.

00:23:05.900 --> 00:23:08.360
I'm sure the same goes for the girls too.

00:23:09.240 --> 00:23:12.780
They're trying their best to learn
 something from others,

00:23:12.780 --> 00:23:14.160
just like Souma-kun.

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:17.160
Damn, we can't be left behind.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:18.620
Let's do a taste-testing festival!

00:23:18.620 --> 00:23:19.710
You guys come too!

00:23:19.710 --> 00:23:20.210
Sure!

00:23:20.210 --> 00:23:21.620
Let's do this!

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:24.590
Not my room again!

00:23:24.590 --> 00:23:26.920
You too, Ibusaki!

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:30.300
You're not going to go with them, Ibusaki-kun?

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.850
Oh, maybe you want to join the girls?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:36.430
You're a closet perv, I see.

00:23:37.430 --> 00:23:40.560
Well, there's no huge rush, though.

00:23:41.350 --> 00:23:46.610
Either way, first-years in our high school division can only relax for a short while.

00:23:47.190 --> 00:23:48.990
Why's that?

00:23:48.990 --> 00:23:49.940
What do you mean?

00:23:50.820 --> 00:23:54.700
Soon, you'll be tossed outside the academy.

00:23:55.700 --> 00:23:56.700
It's going to start.

00:23:56.700 --> 00:24:00.460
The practical training program: the Stagiaire.

00:24:01.040 --> 00:24:02.870
The Stagiaire?

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:09.880
Next time, "The Stagiaire."
